  "name": "Comparing Computer Use Behavior Across Multiple Levels of Abstraction",
  "notes": "Reviewed the complete abstract and selected v1 taxonomy, annotation, evaluation and limitations sections. MAP analyzes existing human/agent traces rather than deploying a new acting policy. Annotation and timing coverage depend on the source datasets; manual agreement reflects a particular labeling scheme. Behavioral findings do not establish a privacy guarantee. No independent reproduction.",
  "published_at": "2026-10-19",
  "relations": [],
  "review_status": "curated",
  "scope": "core",
  "summary": "MAP annotates computer-use traces at linked operation, function/consequence, method and goal levels, then compares human and agent workflows through sequence, pattern and effort metrics.",
